              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new run of words: what did vēr mean, and what did vitai mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: நதி",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "நதி (nadi) — \"a river\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit nadī, and Telugu prints it identically: నది. Malayalam did not take it for the everyday river and says പുഴ (puḻa) instead, which is its own."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Tamil's inherited river is ஆறு — the same shape as the six you already count with. Which of the two is meant comes out of what sits around it, and நதி (nadi) is the one that leaves no room for doubt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five things in a stretch of country."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
