          "title": "You'll want to know: மலை",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "மலை (malai) — \"a hill\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Proto-Dravidian, and it covers a hill and a mountain both — Tamil does not split them the way English does. Telugu keeps a small hill of its own, గుట్ట (guṭṭa)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You have been reading this word all along without being told. The name Malayāḷam begins with it: the language of the hill country, named for its hills."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two: the water, and what it comes down from."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
