          "title": "You'll want to know: வயல்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "வயல் (vayal) — \"a paddy field\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A wet field: the flooded one that grows rice, not a dry one. Malayalam writes വയൽ and means the same thing by it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The dry field is a kollai, a different word altogether, and the split earns its keep. A farmer telling you which of the two he has is telling you what he can grow on it and when."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three: high ground, and now the flat wet ground under it."
            }
          ]
        },
