          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: பாதை",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பாதை (pātai) — \"a path\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Something you can put your foot on: a track worn into the ground, a lane, a road."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Tamil has vaḻi as well, and the two overlap less than they look as though they should. vaḻi is the way — the route, the means, the manner of going about something. பாதை (pātai) stays physical. Malayalam's everyday path-word is വഴി, the same one; Telugu's is bāṭa."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Four: three places, and now something joining them."
            }
          ]
        },
